{{!
    @template local_a11y/face_hud_error

    Face Navigation HUD's error state shell: a translated title, plus an
    empty region for the error detail. The error detail itself is set
    afterwards via .textContent (amd/src/face_navigation.js's renderError()),
    never through this template, because it can carry untrusted text (a
    caught error's own message) - textContent needs no escaping logic to
    get right, unlike interpolating it into markup.

    @description Markup shell for Face Navigation HUD's error state.
    @package    Moodle
    @subpackage Plugin a11y
    @author     Rodrigo Padilha Silveira <padilhars@gmail.com>
    @author     Jerônimo Medina Madruga <jeronimo.madruga@gmail.com>
    @copyright  Universidade Federal de Pelotas - UFPel
    @license    http://www.gnu.org/copyleft/gpl.html GNU GPL v3 or later
    @version    0.1.0
    @since      0.1.0

    Context variables required for this template:
    * errortitle - the already-translated "Error" heading (face_error lang string)

    Example context (json):
    {
        "errortitle": "Error"
    }
}}
<div style="padding:12px">
    <div style="font-weight:600;color:#b91c1c;margin-bottom:2px">{{errortitle}}</div>
    <div data-region="error-msg" style="font-size:11px;color:#6b7280;word-break:break-word"></div>
</div>
